<title>ITALY: Italian airport workers to strike on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Italian airport workers to strike on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian airport workers will hold a one-day strike on Tuesday to protest against lengthy delays in the renewal of wage contracts for the sector, union officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>The strike call has forced state carrier Alitalia to cancel 143 national and international flights scheduled for Tuesday and airport officials said foreign airlines will also be hit by the dispute.</p>
<p>Airport service across Italy will only be guaranteed between 0500-0800 GMT and again between 1600-1900 GMT.</p>
<p>Unions announced the strike in a bid to force the government to replace old pay contracts, which expired in June 1995.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
